e from his brow; it seemed that he truly did have Zhuowu within his breast. Thereafter we met and talked several times, and our talk invariably turned to Old Zhuo. He sought Old Zhuo's surviving words with the greatest eagerness, and sought even more eagerly the books Old Zhuo had annotated and left behind. Could Master Wuya too be mad? Obsessed? I searched my traveling case and found that I had with me the two books Master Zhuowu had edited and settled—the Loyal and Righteous Water Margin and the Collected Works of Yang Sheng'an—so I took them out and handed them to him. Wuya rejoiced as though he had obtained a supreme treasure and wished to make them public to the world. I asked, “Which of the two books should come first?” Wuya said, “The Water Margin is about loyalty and righteousness, and loyalty and righteousness are embodied in the Water Margin. Whether men understand me or condemn me, Old Zhuo's judgment in the manner of the Spring and Autumn Annals lies close to this. Let the Water Margin come first! Let the Water Margin come first!” I laughed and said, “Yes, yes! None but Old Zhuo could reveal the spirit of the Water Margin, and none but Wuya could reveal the spirit of Old Zhuo. I have served Master Zhuowu the longest, yet it is Wuya who has grasped Master Zhuowu most deeply. I am ashamed before Wuya! Yet if not for me, who else could reveal the spirit of Wuya? I have not failed Master Zhuowu, nor has Wuya failed the purpose of my journey here.” Thereupon we looked at each other and laughed, brewed tea and drank together, then took up Master Zhuowu's preface to the Loyal and Righteous Water Margin and read it aloud in unison; the furious waves of the Xu River seemed to answer us. I forgot Wuya, and Wuya forgot me; we knew only that Master Zhuowu existed.","u":[{"en":[["After","","f"]," ",["I","","s"]," ",["traveled","","p"]," ",["to","","f"]," ",["Wu","","d"]," ",["and","","f"]," ",["called","","p"]," ",["upon","","f"]," ",["Governor","","d"]," ",["Chen","